 function has a removable discontinuity at $x=-2.$  Therefore, the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\n- The interval $[0,4]$ is closed, but the function is not defined at $x=0.$ So, it can't be continuous at this point. Therefore, the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\n- The interval $[1,6]$ is closed, and the function is continuous on $[1,6].$ Therefore, the extreme value theorem is applicable.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"III only\"." "Remember that the extreme value theorem is only applicable to closed intervals on which the function is continuous. \n\nWith that in mind, let's take a look at each interval.\n\n- The interval $[-4,-1]$ is closed, but the function has a removable discontinuity at $x=-2.$  Therefore, the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\n- The interval $[0,4]$ is closed, but the function is not defined at $x=0.$ So, it can't be continuous at this point. Therefore, the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\n- The interval $[1,6]$ is closed, and the function is continuous on $[1,6].$ Therefore, the extreme value theorem is applicable.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is $[1,6]$ only."] [:db/cas 17592186464745 :answer-field/key "I" "$[-4,-1]$"] [:db/cas 17592186464746 :answer-field/key "II" "$[0,4]$"] [:db/cas 17592186464747 :answer-field/key "III" "$[1,6]$"] [:db/cas 17592186262693 :question/problem "![](images/3c/3c25115cfb7ccde7ec0cbec249d62b037c7fb94be92905b186101ce1fd45a1d8.png)\n\nConsider the function $y=f(x)$ whose graph is plotted above. On which interval is the extreme value theorem applicable to $f(x)?$\n\nI. $[0,2]$\n\nII. $(1,2)$\n\nIII. $(-\\infty ,0]$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." "![](images/3c/3c25115cfb7ccde7ec0cbec249d62b037c7fb94be92905b186101ce1fd45a1d8.png)\n\nConsider the function $y=f(x)$ whose graph is plotted above. On which interval is the extreme value theorem applicable to $f(x)?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked."] [:db/cas 17592186262693 :question/worked-solution "Remember that the extreme value theorem is only applicable to closed intervals on which the function is continuous.\n\nWith that in mind, let's take a look at each interval.\n\n- The interval $[0,2]$ is closed, and the function is continuous on $[0,2].$ Therefore, the extreme value theorem is applicable.\n\n- The interval $(1,2)$ is not closed, so the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\n- The interval $(-\\infty ,0]$ is closed, but it is not a bounded interval in the form $[a,b].$ Therefore, the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"I only\"." "Remember that the extreme value theorem is only applicable to closed intervals on which the function is continuous.\n\nWith that in mind, let's take a look at each interval.\n\n- The interval $[0,2]$ is closed, and the function is continuous on $[0,2].$ Therefore, the extreme value theorem is applicable.\n\n- The interval $(1,2)$ is not closed, so the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\n- The interval $(-\\infty ,0]$ is closed, but it is not a bounded interval in the form $[a,b].$ Therefore, the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is $[0,2]$ only."] [:db/cas 17592186464748 :answer-field/key "I" "$[0,2]$"] [:db/cas 17592186464749 :answer-field/key "II" "$(1,2)$"] [:db/cas 17592186464750 :answer-field/key "III" "$(-\\infty ,0]$"] [:db/cas 17592186262822 :question/problem "Which of the matrices below are singular?\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." "Which of the matrices below are singular?\n\nSelect all that apply."] [:db/cas 17592186464751 :answer-field/key "A" "$A=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$"] [:db/cas 17592186464752 :answer-field/key "B" "$B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$"] [:db/cas 17592186464753 :answer-field/key "C" "$C=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$"] [:db/cas 17592186262823 :question/problem "Which of the matrices below does **not** have an inverse?\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." "Which of the matrices below does **not** have an inverse?\n\nSelect all that apply."] [:db/cas 17592186464754 :answer-field/key "A" "$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$"] [:db/cas 17592186464755 :answer-field/key "B" "$B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$"] [:db/cas 17592186464756 :answer-field/key "C" "$C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$"] [:db/cas 17592186262824 :question/problem "Which of the matrices below are singular?\n\n$$\nS=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,T=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -6\\end{bmatrix},\\,U=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." "Which of the matrices below are singular?\n\nSelect all that apply."] [:db/cas 17592186464757 :answer-field/key "S" "$S=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$"] [:db/cas 17592186464758 :answer-field/key "T" "$T=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -6\\end{bmatrix}$"] [:db/cas 17592186464759 :answer-field/key "U" "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$"] [:db/cas 17592186262825 :question/problem "Which of the matrices below does **not** have an inverse?\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 12 \\\\ 3 & 9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." "Which of the matrices below does **not** have an inverse?\n\nSelect all that apply."] [:db/cas 17592186464760 :answer-field/key "A" "$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$"] [:db/cas 17592186464761 :answer-field/key "B" "$B=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 3 \\\\ 